# Code owners for Sproutwall. See GOVERNANCE.md and
# docs/maintainers/repo-setup.md, section 5.
#
# With "Require review from Code Owners" on, a pull request needs an approval
# from an owner of every file it changes, and GitHub never lets authors
# approve their own pull requests.
#
# @hjunk is the human maintainer. He reviews and approves pull requests from
# contributors and Dependabot.
# @ari-hjunk is his AI agent reviewer account. By project rule (GitHub does
# not enforce this), it approves only pull requests opened by @hjunk (written
# by his AI agents), and only after an independent AI review passed at that
# exact commit. Its approval means "an agent review passed", not a human
# review. @hjunk merges.
# .github/ (workflows, rules and this file) and GOVERNANCE.md are owned by
# @hjunk alone.
# Later rules win over earlier ones.

# Default owners for everything.
*                       @hjunk @ari-hjunk

# Sensitive paths: access control, PIN, outbound fetches, the assistant
# bridge, the container and scripts. Keep these owned by the core
# maintainers only, even after skill owners or other maintainers are added
# to the default rule above.
/src/app/api/**         @hjunk @ari-hjunk
/src/proxy.ts           @hjunk @ari-hjunk
/src/lib/session.ts     @hjunk @ari-hjunk
/src/lib/guard.ts       @hjunk @ari-hjunk
/src/lib/auth.ts        @hjunk @ari-hjunk
/src/lib/pin-attempts.ts @hjunk @ari-hjunk
/src/lib/safe-fetch.ts  @hjunk @ari-hjunk
/bridge/**              @hjunk @ari-hjunk
/Dockerfile             @hjunk @ari-hjunk
/docker-compose*.yml    @hjunk @ari-hjunk
/docker/**              @hjunk @ari-hjunk
/scripts/**             @hjunk @ari-hjunk

# Repository automation and these rules: the human maintainer only.
/.github/**             @hjunk
/GOVERNANCE.md          @hjunk
